# Ingestion & Deconstruction (Stage 1) Implementation Plan

## Goal Description
Implement the "Gateway" for PhishVault-2, responsible for ingesting, normalizing, and deconstructing artifacts (URLs, Emails, Files). This involves creating a unified Ingestion Engine that uses a Factory pattern to handle different input types, canonicalizes URLs, and decomposes composite artifacts like emails into their components.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> The existing [submitEmailHandler](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori%20Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/services/ingestion/main.go#93-130) and [submitHandler](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori%20Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/services/ingestion/main.go#52-92) in [services/ingestion/main.go](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori%20Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/services/ingestion/main.go) will be significantly refactored to use the new `engine` package.

## Proposed Changes

### Service: Ingestion
I will create a new package `services/ingestion/engine` to encapsulate the logic.

#### [NEW] [types.go](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/services/ingestion/engine/types.go)
- Define `IngestedArtifact` struct.
- Define `ArtifactType` enum (URL, EMAIL, FILE).
- Define `Processor` interface.

#### [NEW] [factory.go](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/services/ingestion/engine/factory.go)
- Implement `ArtifactFactory` to select the correct processor based on input type.
- Implement `Ingest(ctx, input)` method that orchestrates hashing, processing, and storage.

#### [NEW] [canonicalizer.go](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/services/ingestion/engine/canonicalizer.go)
- Implement `CanonicalizeURL(url string) (string, Metadata)`
- Punycode decoding.
- Parameter stripping (utm_, etc).
- Redirect unwinding (using `net/http` client with limits).

#### [NEW] [email_processor.go](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/services/ingestion/engine/email_processor.go)
- Implement `Process(artifact)` for Emails.
- Parse EML/MSG.
- Extract Headers (X-Headers, Authentication results).
- Deconstruct into Body and Attachments.
- Return list of child artifacts (Links, Attachments).

#### [NEW] [attachment_processor.go](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/services/ingestion/engine/attachment_processor.go)
- Implement `Process(artifact)` for Files.
- Calculate Hashes (SHA256, MD5).
- Magic number file type detection.
- Extract text/URLs if applicable (basic regex for now).

#### [MODIFY] [main.go](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/services/ingestion/main.go)
- Initialize `ArtifactFactory`.
- Update [submitHandler](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori%20Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/services/ingestion/main.go#52-92) to use `Factory.Ingest(URL)`.
- Update [submitEmailHandler](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori%20Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/services/ingestion/main.go#93-130) to use `Factory.Ingest(Email)`.
- Ensure data is persisted to DB/MinIO and dispatched to RabbitMQ via the new structure.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- **Unit Tests**: Create [_test.go](file:///c:/Users/Kandukoori%20Tejaswini/Desktop/PhishVault2/PhishVault/services/storage/verification_test.go) files for each new processor.
    - `canonicalizer_test.go`: Test various URL formats, punycode, redirects.
    - `email_processor_test.go`: Parse sample .eml files and verify child artifacts.
    - `factory_test.go`: Verify correct processor selection and workflow.
- **Integration Test**:
    - Run the ingestion service.
    - Submit a complex Email via `curl` or a Go test script.
    - Verify in Postgres (scans table) and MinIO (artifacts) that the email and its children (attachments/links) are stored.

### Manual Verification
1.  **URL Submission**: Submit a known tracking URL (e.g. with `utm_source`) and verify it is stripped in the DB.
2.  **Email Submission**: Submit a `.eml` file with an attachment. Verify:
    -   Email is stored.
    -   Attachment is stored as a separate artifact with `parent_id` pointing to the email.
